@startuml
title OmniDesk Deployment Architecture

left to right direction
skinparam nodeStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "User Device" as Device {
  artifact "Web Browser" as Browser
}

node "Application Host" as Host {
  node "Web Server" as WebServer {
    artifact "React Web Client" as Client
  }

  node "Application Runtime" as Runtime {
    artifact "Laravel REST API" as API
    artifact "Background Worker" as Worker
    artifact "TDLib Adapter" as TDLib
    folder "Private per-user Telegram runtimes" as TelegramSessions
  }
}

node "Data Services" as Data {
  database "PostgreSQL" as DB
  node "Redis" as Redis
}

cloud "External Services" as External {
  component "Gmail API" as Gmail
  component "Telegram API" as Telegram
}

Browser --> Client : HTTPS
Client --> API : REST / JSON over HTTPS
API --> DB : durable data
API --> Redis : cache or job state
API --> Worker : dispatch background job
Worker --> Redis : queue processing
Worker --> DB : synchronization and audit data
Worker --> Gmail : provider requests
Worker --> Telegram : provider requests
API --> TDLib : owner-scoped authorization and reads
TDLib --> TelegramSessions : isolated encrypted session state
TDLib --> Telegram : MTProto / TDLib requests

note right of DB
Stores application data and protected
connection information, including encrypted
Telegram phone values and database keys.
end note

note right of External
External services remain outside the
OmniDesk deployment boundary.
end note

note bottom of Host
The initial deployment may use a single
application host with separate web,
runtime, and worker processes.
end note

@enduml
